{
  "description": "Compaction changes model context without hiding the saved transcript. Updated 2026-10-03 because the previous renderer clipped every message before the latest boundary and reset its disclosure on each compaction start. Cold-opening a saved session immediately shows its latest real user message and replies, including long turns that span compaction; compaction, file restore and summary rows cannot replace the real turn opener as a pagination boundary. Primary and read-only transcripts keep message order across all boundaries; only restored file contents require disclosure. Earlier turns continue to use normal upward pagination. Updated 2026-10-27: the checkpoint body the engine persists for prompt context (assistant text tagged with the compaction-output envelope) is provider context, never a visible reply; the host projection skips it and the saved boundary renders as the compaction divider alone, with no summary body anywhere in the desktop transcript. The renderer keeps its summary-card row kind for surfaces that produce it (the mobile live stream); the desktop host never emits it.",
